    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "The Words of Agur"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The words of Agur son of Jakeh. The pronouncement. ,",
          "The man’s oration to Ithiel, to Ithiel and Ucal:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I am more stupid than any other person,",
          "and I lack a human’s ability to understand."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I have not gained wisdom,",
          "and I have no knowledge of the Holy One."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who has gone up to heaven and come down?",
          "Who has gathered the wind in his hands?",
          "Who has bound up the waters in a cloak?",
          "Who has established all the ends of the earth?",
          "What is his name,",
          "and what is the name of his son —",
          "if you know?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Every word of God is pure; ,",
          "he is a shield to those who take refuge in him."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Don’t add to his words,",
          "or he will rebuke you, and you will be proved a liar."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Two things I ask of you;",
          "don’t deny them to me before I die:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Keep falsehood and deceitful words far from me.",
          "Give me neither poverty nor wealth;",
          "feed me with the food I need."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Otherwise, I might have too much",
          "and deny you, saying, “Who is the Lord? ”",
          "or I might have nothing and steal,",
          "profaning the name of my God."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Don’t slander a servant to his master",
          "or he will curse you, and you will become guilty."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "There is a generation that curses its father",
          "and does not bless its mother."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "There is a generation that is pure in its own eyes,",
          "yet is not washed from its filth."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "There is a generation #— #how haughty its eyes",
          "and pretentious its looks."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "There is a generation whose teeth are swords,",
          "whose fangs are knives,",
          "devouring the oppressed from the land",
          "and the needy from among mankind."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The leech has two daughters: “Give, Give! ”",
          "Three things are never satisfied;",
          "four never say, “Enough! ”:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Sheol; a childless womb;",
          "earth, which is never satisfied with water;",
          "and fire, which never says, “Enough! ”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "As for the eye that ridicules a father",
          "and despises obedience to a mother,",
          "may ravens of the valley pluck it out",
          "and young vultures eat it."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Three things are too wondrous for me;",
          "four I can’t understand:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "the way of an eagle in the sky,",
          "the way of a snake on a rock,",
          "the way of a ship at sea,",
          "and the way of a man with a young woman."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "This is the way of an adulteress:",
          "she eats and wipes her mouth",
          "and says, “I’ve done nothing wrong.”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          21
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The earth trembles under three things;",
          "it cannot bear up under four:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          22
        ],
        "lines": [
          "a servant when he becomes king,",
          "a fool when he is stuffed with food,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          23
        ],
        "lines": [
          "an unloved woman when she marries,",
          "and a servant girl when she ousts her queen."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          24
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Four things on earth are small,",
          "yet they are extremely wise:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          25
        ],
        "lines": [
          "ants are not a strong people,",
          "yet they store up their food in the summer;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          26
        ],
        "lines": [
          "hyraxes are not a mighty people,",
          "yet they make their homes in the cliffs;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          27
        ],
        "lines": [
          "locusts have no king,",
          "yet all of them march in ranks;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          28
        ],
        "lines": [
          "a lizard can be caught in your hands,",
          "yet it lives in kings’ palaces."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          29
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Three things are stately in their stride;",
          "four are stately in their walk:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          30
        ],
        "lines": [
          "a lion, which is mightiest among beasts",
          "and doesn’t retreat before anything;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          31
        ],
        "lines": [
          "a strutting rooster; a goat;",
          "and a king at the head of his army."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          32
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If you have been foolish by exalting yourself",
          "or if you’ve been scheming,",
          "put your hand over your mouth."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          33
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For the churning of milk produces butter,",
          "and twisting a nose draws blood,",
          "and stirring up anger produces strife."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
